<title>UK: J.Menzies to buy prefshares at 112p maximum.</title>
<headline>J.Menzies to buy prefshares at 112p maximum.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Menzies Plc said on Thursday it would purchase nine percent cumulative preference shares of one stg each at a price not exceeding 112 pence per share.</p>
<p>That is 103.7 percent of the average middle market quotation for the last 10 business days.</p>
<p>The company had already sought shareholder approval on the purchase at its annual meeting on September, 6, 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;The company is prepared to make purchases on the above basis during the period from the date of this announcement until April 30, 1997,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
